test: require the legacy wallet and its migration warning

If `listwalletdir` omits the wallet, the loop never checks its warning and the test passes.
The loop also skips `path/to/trailing/` because the listed name has no trailing separator.

Match the wallet by its listed name and require the migration warning.
With the following mutation, the original test passes and the new check fails because `basic0` is missing.

```diff
diff --git a/src/wallet/db.cpp b/src/wallet/db.cpp
index 3af0f1ca41..40a9917873 100644
--- a/src/wallet/db.cpp
+++ b/src/wallet/db.cpp
@@ -34,5 +34,4 @@ std::vector<std::pair<fs::path, std::string>> ListDatabases(const fs::path& wall
                 if (IsBDBFile(BDBDataFile(it->path()))) {
                     // Found a directory which contains wallet.dat btree file, add it as a wallet with BERKELEY format.
-                    paths.emplace_back(path, "bdb");
                 } else if (IsSQLiteFile(SQLiteDataFile(it->path()))) {
                     // Found a directory which contains wallet.dat sqlite file, add it as a wallet with SQLITE format.
```

test: check that `listwalletdir` omits migration backups

Every wallet returned by `listwalletdir` has a `warnings` field, so checking that `{"name": backup_filename}` is absent passes even when the backup is listed.
Compare the backup filename with the listed names instead.

Removing the `.bak` filter makes `listwalletdir` return the backup, which the previous test accepts and the new check catches.

```diff
diff --git a/src/wallet/db.cpp b/src/wallet/db.cpp
index 3af0f1ca41..a2d41065ec 100644
--- a/src/wallet/db.cpp
+++ b/src/wallet/db.cpp
@@ -39,5 +39,5 @@ std::vector<std::pair<fs::path, std::string>> ListDatabases(const fs::path& wall
                     paths.emplace_back(path, "sqlite");
                 }
-            } else if (it.depth() == 0 && it->symlink_status().type() == fs::file_type::regular && it->path().extension() != ".bak") {
+            } else if (it.depth() == 0 && it->symlink_status().type() == fs::file_type::regular) {
                 if (it->path().filename() == "wallet.dat") {
                     // Found top-level wallet.dat file, add top level directory ""
```

test: check wrapped P2WSH addresses after wallet migration

The test imports a `sh(wsh(pkh()))` output but only calls `getaddressinfo` on the native P2WSH address after migration.
Check that the migrated wallet owns both forms and reports the embedded script for each.

With this mutation, `getaddressinfo` omits `embedded` for the wrapped address while still returning it for the native address.

```diff
diff --git a/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp b/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp
index 3470bceee7..f85951a34f 100644
--- a/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp
+++ b/src/wallet/rpc/addresses.cpp
@@ -319,5 +319,5 @@ public:
         UniValue obj(UniValue::VOBJ);
         CScript subscript;
-        if (provider && provider->GetCScript(ToScriptID(scripthash), subscript)) {
+        if (provider && provider->GetCScript(ToScriptID(scripthash), subscript) && !subscript.IsPayToWitnessScriptHash()) {
             ProcessSubScript(subscript, obj);
         }
```
